Signed-off-by: Dennis Dalessandro <dennis.dalessandro@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Doug Ledford <dledford@redhat.com>

Here is the root cause:
The use of a global variable `qpt_mask` did not support the multiple chip model of the qib driver, leading to potential conflicts and incorrect behavior when multiple devices were in use. This design flaw could result in incorrect handling of queue pair numbers across different devices, as the global state would not reflect the specific configuration of each device instance.

